foreign  [Music]  do you deal with monotonous  time-consuming administrative tasks that  come with certificate management well  you're not alone and until now issuance  and renewals of private certificates had  to be manually managed come along as we  explore how certificate Authority  service and certificate Manager work  together to simplify this process for  you managing the life cycle of your  private certificates for workloads like  Mutual TLS or private pki isn't always a  walk in the park  even when they're centralized you still  have to deal with manually issuing and  provisioning your private certificates  to your load balancers and you have to  consider all of this before your  certificates expire and renewals come up  the good news is you don't have to do it  all manually when using Cas with  certificate manager now you can have  your private certificates fully managed  by certificate manager CCM with Cas CA  pools issuing the certificates when  using this combo certificates are  automatically issued and provisioned to  your load balancer and renewed without  you needing to keep track or manually  manage that renewal this is how it works  Cas houses the ca pool that issues the  certificates CCM gives you fine control  over the issuance and provisioning of  certificates to your load balancers  without manual intervention  you can configure the managed  certificate resource with the load  balancer once and then certificate  manager takes care of issuing new  certificates and provisioning them to  the load balancer according to your  configuration plus everything is  centralized so you have one place to  manage your certificates across your  Google services  this allows you to manage and serve  larger numbers of certificates and  therefore put time and resources towards  more pressing tasks like managing your  business there are four easy steps to  provision and deploy certificates from  Cas make sure you have the ca admin  compute load balancer admin and  certificate manager owner roles before  you begin  first you'll need to create a CA pool  with at least one enabled CA or use one  that you currently have then create a  certificate issuance configuration this  is where you'll specify which pool to  use to provision your certificates this  is also the time to specify other  configurable variables like certificate  lifetime renewal period and key  algorithm next create a managed  certificate this is where you can  specify that you want a Google manage  certificate which means that Google  Cloud obtains and manages them for you  and again this managed certificate will  be configured to use the casca pool you  identified in the previous configuration  step finally attach your managed  certificate to your load balancer this  step gives certificate manager the  authorization to obtain provision and  renew your certificates to your load  balancer CCM will request the actual  certificates from Cas and provision them  to the load balancer once you do these  steps your private certificate  management is taken care of for you and  you no longer have to worry about  renewals if you'd like to know more  about having your certificates fully  managed with CCM and Cas check out the  links listed in the description below if  you enjoyed the video give us a like and  let us know your thoughts in the  comments until next time thanks for  watching  [Music]  thank you

